From f44cde961fe136deb4db285a7e8185dcdb988dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: red-Geck0 <127088086+red-Geck0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:04:57 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 71/72] feat(framegen): FSR frame generation on GPUs with one
 graphics queue (Intel Arc)

AMD FSR frame generation (patch 0055) needs three queues besides the game
queue, taken from the graphics family. Intel Arc has a single graphics
queue, so frame generation never started there; with that fixed, the FSR
runtime still failed to create its context on Intel's driver.

- A graphics family with too few queues gives FSR three queues of a
  compute family that can present to the window instead (family 1 on
  Arc). FSR's swapchain gets each queue's family; the interpolation then
  runs on the game queue (ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG_ASYNC=1 to try async compute),
  so Kyty's images are not used from another queue family.
- FSR's descriptor pools ask for up to 16,000 sets of 512 descriptors of
  each type (8,192,000); Intel's driver refuses them with
  VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY and the context creation failed with
  FFX_API_RETURN_ERROR_RUNTIME_ERROR (3). FSR 3.1.6 frame generation uses
  720 sets in all (largest 19 descriptors), so vkCreateDescriptorPool is
  wrapped to ask again for at most 4096 / 2048 / 1024 sets of 32
  descriptors per type. If FSR still fails to allocate a set
  (VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_POOL_MEMORY), its context is dropped and frame
  generation turns off: running it without its sets froze the game.
- FSR's graphics pipelines have a static line width of 0 (needs
  wideLines, VUID-VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo-pDynamicStates-00749); it
  is set to 1.
- Failures of the other Vulkan calls FSR makes, and device functions it
  cannot get, are printed: the runtime itself only returns an error code.
- The frame generation versions the runtime offers are listed and tried
  newest first (ASTROHYBRID_FSRFG_VERSION=<prefix> picks one), then
  without async workload support.
- If creating the context for a render size above the display size (the
  game's 3840x2160 menus in a smaller window) fails, the display size
  becomes the cap and larger frames are shown without generation (skip
  "above-display"), instead of frame generation turning off for the
  session. Contexts that can be created are sized as before.

Tested on Intel Arc B390 (MSI Claw 8 EX, Intel driver 101.9175), 1920x1094
window, full overlay: with FSR upscaling and with XeSS upscaling, the
context is created on version 3.1.6 (render up to 3840x2160) with its
refused pools at 4096 sets,
every game frame gets a generated one (220/220 and 280/280 per 10 s) for
over two minutes, 45 FPS on screen with the game at 22 FPS (FSR), picture
and HUD correct, clean exit.
